Z||000000||SibERThuG||07-08-2000||01:41 AM||||I am about to get airbag suspension so I can raise/lower my car when needed and more easily. Has anyone ever done this with their fiero? Any problems with it??||||reg||2
Z||000001||Monkeyman||07-08-2000||09:19 AM||||Why would you want to spend lots of $$, time, effort, etc just to raise the car?  If you want it lowered, just buy/install some lowering springs.  If you want to raise it to work on it, buy a good floor jack and some jack stands.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||07-11-2000||11:28 AM||||I have looked at those a little.<BR>You will have to have the wheels aligned at a ride height that you will use all the time or you will go through tires like crazy.  Then you can drop it down for shows and raise it up to go into driveways.  Also if you have sway bars you might have some problems with them interfering with the raising and lowering of the car. <BR>Do they even make them to fit a Fiero? <BR>When you start or do the install please contact me and or post it Here.||||reg||1
Z||000003||dman||07-11-2000||01:55 PM||||Hi SibERThuG. Like Spyder said, if you do come across any information (part numbers, vendors, prices, etc) please post it here. I'm sure many of use, like myself, would be interested to find out more. Thanks!||||reg||1
